From 790bbf0689192056698db247f391ee89cbe128b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raimondas Lencevicius <59739769+raimondasl@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:10:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] Support harness summary compaction in manual_rolling

manual_rolling drops the oldest user/assistant pair once the estimated
transcript size exceeds MAX_CONTEXT_LENGTH, and config validation rejected
runtime.compaction outside continuous_conversation, so a Standard
(visible-text) run could not use the Provider Adapter's loss policy.

- ManualRollingSummaryAdapter presents the agent-owned text transcript to
  the existing SummaryCompactor through the configured plain API adapter.
  A user message followed by its assistant reply is one accepted turn;
  buffered observations (GAME_OVER before a forced RESET) and the bridge
  sit between turns, as in the Google adapter, so summary-overflow
  unwinding works unchanged.
- The agent schedules compaction from the accepted request's own
  provider-reported total_tokens (not the retry sum), runs it before the
  next model turn, and replaces the transcript with the system prompt and
  the user-role bridge. Action-request context overflow compacts the
  accepted history and keeps the current observation pending, once.
- Compaction usage, compaction_NNN.json, the step continuation record and
  action-metadata attribution reuse the continuous-conversation code.
- Config validation accepts harness_summary on manual_rolling with the
  same trigger/output/headroom reserve check; previous_response_id still
  rejects runtime.compaction.
- run_meta.json gains a runtime block for these configs, including
  context_trims, which counts oldest-turn drops (the backstop that should
  not fire when MAX_CONTEXT_LENGTH is the provider's context capacity).

Configs without runtime.compaction are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
